# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_render_dampening_honest.py" "DAMPENING-HONEST RENDER GATE: PASS" "render dampening-honest" "render dampening-honest (a non-empty dampened_with on ANY non-'unknown' verdict downgrades to honest 'unknown' so the suppression is silence-visible; the comment NAMES the hub file + says 'treat as unknown, not clear'; round-trip baseline without the dampened signal still renders clear; corroborated dampening still earns its 'two independent signals' warn — never re-flattened)" "render dampening-honest: an engine-leaked 'clear' carrying an uncorroborated dampened_with row never rides through as a silent green check → the renderer downgrades to 'unknown' and surfaces the hub file by name; the corroborated AUDIT3 relaxation is preserved" 20
